  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Pretrained Weights are the learned parameter tensors of a neural network obtained by training on a large corpus prior to task-specific adaptation. They encode generalised representations\u2014syntactic, semantic, visual, or domain knowledge\u2014that downstream tasks can exploit through fine-tuning or zero-shot inference, dramatically reducing the data and compute required to achieve strong performance on new problems.",
